## 2026-02-22 Update - USB GPS (G-Mouse DL28U9U) Pipeline

### New gateway artifacts

- Adapter contract added: `src/adapters/gps.ts`
  - `GpsChipset`, `GpsConfig`, `GpsFix`, `GpsAdapter`
- Adapter export added in `src/adapters/index.ts`.

### Raspberry Pi runtime scripts

Folder: `rpi/omi-imu/`

- `01_test_gps.py`: reads USB serial NMEA and prints parsed fix data.
- `02_publish_gps_signalk.py`: parses NMEA (RMC/GGA/GSA/GSV/VTG), converts units, and publishes to Signal K.
- `setup_gps.sh`: detects GPS serial device, installs dependencies, probes raw NMEA stream.

Dependencies used on RPi:

- `pyserial`
- `pynmea2`
- `requests`
- `websocket-client`

### Signal K paths published by GPS script

- `navigation.position`
- `navigation.speedOverGround`
- `navigation.courseOverGroundTrue`
- `navigation.magneticVariation`
- `navigation.datetime`
- `sensors.gps.fix`
- `sensors.gps.satellitesInView`
- `sensors.gps.horizontalDilution`

### Unit conversion rules

- SOG: knots -> m/s (`* 0.514444`)
- COG true: degrees -> radians
- Magnetic variation: degrees -> radians, East positive / West negative

### Runtime behavior observed in validated environment

Validation date: 2026-02-22.

- USB GPS detected as `/dev/ttyACM0` on Raspberry Pi.
- NMEA stream present and parseable.
- HTTP write endpoints were not available in tested Signal K instance (`404/405`).
- WebSocket publish fallback to `/signalk/v1/stream?subscribe=none` succeeded.

### Verified read endpoints

- `/signalk/v1/api/vessels/self/navigation/position`
- `/signalk/v1/api/vessels/self/navigation/speedOverGround`
- `/signalk/v1/api/vessels/self/navigation/datetime`
- `/signalk/v1/api/vessels/self/sensors/gps`

IMU and GPS publishers were validated running simultaneously.
